import Placeholder from '../components/Placeholder.astro';
import WorkPage from '../layouts/WorkPage.astro';
---

<WorkPage
	title="Homeroll"
	description="A private photo stream for my family. In production; built end to end in TypeScript."
>
	<h1>Homeroll — <a href="https://homeroll.app">homeroll.app</a></h1>
	<p class="repo"><a href="https://github.com/reharik/photo-app">github.com/reharik/photo-app</a></p>

	<p>
		My extended family is spread across every platform, and some are on none. So photos get shared
		by text, and fifteen minutes later they're lost in the thread. I wanted a place we could share
		them without putting the family on a social feed, and without confusing the heck out of my aunts
		in the old country.
	</p>
	<p>
		Homeroll is a private family photo stream. Anyone can sign up and upload, and nobody sees
		anything that hasn't been shared with them directly. It's built against the threats that
		actually matter for family photos: nothing indexed or crawlable, nothing sold or trained on, no
		feed. Share links exist because people need them, but they're unguessable, you can see who has
		one, and you can revoke it. It is not locked down like a bank, because then nobody's aunt would
		use it. And it has every feature I ever wanted.
	</p>

	<div class="shots">
		<Placeholder block label="Homeroll screenshot 1" path="src/assets/work/homeroll-screenshot-1.png" />
		<Placeholder block label="Homeroll screenshot 2" path="src/assets/work/homeroll-screenshot-2.png" />
		<Placeholder block label="Homeroll screenshot 3" path="src/assets/work/homeroll-screenshot-3.png" />
		<Placeholder block label="Homeroll screenshot 4 (optional)" path="src/assets/work/homeroll-screenshot-4.png" />
	</div>

	<h2>How it's built</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>TypeScript end to end</li>
		<li>Domain-driven design: domain events, repositories, async services</li>
		<li>
			Dependency injection via ioc-manifest and typed enums via smart-enums, both battle-tested here
			before publishing
		</li>
		<li>React, Node, Postgres, S3; Nx monorepo, Vite, Playwright e2e</li>
		<li>Installable on phones as a PWA</li>
		<li>Self-hosted on AWS behind Caddy, containers deployed via GitHub Actions</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		<strong>The hard part:</strong> the photo pipeline. An upload kicks off optimization, storage, and
		notifications, each async and each able to fail on its own. Keeping that lifecycle coherent while
		surfacing it to the user, then deep-linking in-app notifications back into it: that's where most
		of the real engineering went.
	</p>
</WorkPage>

<style>
	.repo {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
	}
	.shots {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16rem), 1fr));
		gap: 1rem;
	}
</style>
